     1,
     "<div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">Hello,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">I am trying to figure out how to specify a simple latent variable model for ranking data in <span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">lavaan</span> based on <a href=\"http://10.1037/1082-989X.10.3.285\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://10.1037/1082-989X.10.3.285&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414358551000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15NE6vMyi1cY7B3FjhJ5Av\">Maydeu-Olivares and Bockenholt, 2005</a>. I am wondering if I am missing some constraints or some scaling factors because the mean structure doesn’t match what I am expecting. Here are the details:</p>\r\n<span style=\"margin:1.3em 0px 1em;padding:0px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.4em;border-bottom:1px solid rgb(238,238,238)\">Simulations</span>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">I first simulated some latent utilities from independent normals with unique means and variances equal to 1. I then converted these to ranks based on the order statistics. From there, I created ordered indicators based on pairs. That is, if item 1 is ranked ahead of item 2, the indicator i1i2 gets a 1, and zero otherwise.</p>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248);display:block\">set.seed(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">5663</span>)\r\nmu &lt;- c(-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">4</span>, -<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>, -<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>)\r\n\r\nranks &lt;- sapply(\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">100</span>,\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(x){\r\n    s &lt;- rnorm(length(mu), mean = mu)\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">return</span>(order(s))\r\n  }\r\n) |&gt; t()\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># give names</span>\r\ncolnames(ranks) &lt;- paste0(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">4</span>)\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># create indexes</span>\r\nindexes &lt;- list()\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span>(i <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:(ncol(ranks) - <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>)){\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span>(j <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> (i+<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>):ncol(ranks)){\r\n    indexes &lt;- c(\r\n      indexes,\r\n      list(c(i, j))\r\n    )\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># convert to pairs data</span>\r\npairs_dat &lt;- matrix(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>, nrow = nrow(ranks), ncol = choose(ncol(ranks), <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>))\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span>(i <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:nrow(pairs_dat)){\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">for</span>(j <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:ncol(pairs_dat)){\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">if</span>(ranks[i, indexes[[j]][<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>]] &lt; ranks[i, indexes[[j]][<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>]]){\r\n      pairs_dat[i, j] &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># give better names</span>\r\ncolnames(pairs_dat) &lt;- c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i1i2&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i1i3&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i1i4&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i2i3&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i2i4&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;i3i4&quot;</span>)\r\npairs_dat &lt;- as.data.frame(pairs_dat)\r\n</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"margin:1.3em 0px 1em;padding:0px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.4em;border-bottom:1px solid rgb(238,238,238)\">Fitting the model</span>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">Based on the simple case 5 model, I constrain the latent variables to have  variances of 1 and to be orthogonal. I also specify a mean structure, and constrain one of the latent means to zero for identifiability. I also want to specify that the indicators are observed without error since the ranks data are intransitive and imply a specific order. Here is the model specification.</p>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248);display:block\"><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># specify model components</span>\r\nreg &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;\r\n  i1 ~ 1 \r\n  i2 ~ 1\r\n  i3 ~ 1\r\n  i4 ~ 0 * 1\r\n&#39;</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># fix the factor loadings as pairwise differences</span>\r\nmeas &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;\r\n  i1 =~ 1 * i1i2 + 1 * i1i3 + 1 * i1i4\r\n  i2 =~ -1 * i1i2 + 1 * i2i3 + 1 * i2i4\r\n  i3 =~ -1 * i1i3 + -1 * i2i3 + 1 * i3i4\r\n  i4 =~ -1 * i1i4 + -1 * i2i4 + -1 * i3i4\r\n&#39;</span>\r\n\r\ncovars &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;\r\n  # residual variances constrained\r\n  i1i2 ~~ 0 * i1i2\r\n  i1i3 ~~ 0 * i1i3\r\n  i1i4 ~~ 0 * i1i4\r\n  i2i3 ~~ 0 * i2i3\r\n  i2i4 ~~ 0 * i2i4\r\n  i3i4 ~~ 0 * i3i4\r\n&#39;</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># fit the model</span>\r\nmfit &lt;- lavaan(\r\n  model = c(reg, meas, covars),\r\n  data = pairs_dat,\r\n  ordered = names(pairs_dat)[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">6</span>],\r\n  parameterization = <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;theta&quot;</span>,\r\n  meanstructure = <span>T</span>,\r\n  orthogonal = <span>T</span>,\r\n  <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414358551000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ISuxrM6fPf18lOrk3Hb-z\">std.lv</a> = <span>T</span>\r\n)\r\n\r\nsummary(mfit)\r\n</span></span>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block\">lavaan 0.6-18 ended normally after 10 iterations\r\n\r\n  Estimator                                       DWLS\r\n  Optimization method                           NLMINB\r\n  Number of model parameters                         3\r\n\r\n  Number of observations                           100\r\n\r\nModel Test User Model:\r\n                                              Standard      Scaled\r\n  Test Statistic                                36.119      30.665\r\n  Degrees of freedom                                18          18\r\n  P-value (Chi-square)                           0.007       0.031\r\n  Scaling correction factor                                  1.513\r\n  Shift parameter                                            6.788\r\n    simple second-order correction                                \r\n\r\nParameter Estimates:\r\n\r\n  Parameterization                               Theta\r\n  Standard errors                           Robust.sem\r\n  Information                                 Expected\r\n  Information saturated (h1) model        Unstructured\r\n\r\nLatent Variables:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n  i1 =~                                               \r\n    i1i2              1.000                           \r\n    i1i3              1.000                           \r\n    i1i4              1.000                           \r\n  i2 =~                                               \r\n    i1i2             -1.000                           \r\n    i2i3              1.000                           \r\n    i2i4              1.000                           \r\n  i3 =~                                               \r\n    i1i3             -1.000                           \r\n    i2i3             -1.000                           \r\n    i3i4              1.000                           \r\n  i4 =~                                               \r\n    i1i4             -1.000                           \r\n    i2i4             -1.000                           \r\n    i3i4             -1.000                           \r\n\r\nIntercepts:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n    i1                0.942    0.226    4.170    0.000\r\n    i2                0.632    0.202    3.132    0.002\r\n    i3                0.365    0.178    2.051    0.040\r\n    i4                0.000                           \r\n\r\nThresholds:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n    i1i2|t1          -0.772                           \r\n    i1i3|t1          -1.341                           \r\n    i1i4|t1          -2.326                           \r\n    i2i3|t1          -0.739                           \r\n    i2i4|t1          -1.405                           \r\n    i3i4|t1          -0.954                           \r\n\r\nVariances:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n   .i1i2              0.000                           \r\n   .i1i3              0.000                           \r\n   .i1i4              0.000                           \r\n   .i2i3              0.000                           \r\n   .i2i4              0.000                           \r\n   .i3i4              0.000                           \r\n    i1                1.000                           \r\n    i2                1.000                           \r\n    i3                1.000                           \r\n    i4                1.000                           \r\n\r\nScales y*:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n    i1i2              0.707                           \r\n    i1i3              0.707                           \r\n    i1i4              0.707                           \r\n    i2i3              0.707                           \r\n    i2i4              0.707                           \r\n    i3i4              0.707\r\n</span></span><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">The resulting summary of the model looks mostly as expected, but I haven’t been able to figure out why the latent means aren’t anywhere near the means I specified in the simulation. I also can’t figure out how to get from the estimated means to the thresholds. My understanding was that the threshold relationship should be</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/GChEffVOJyFgj4qeEAgRLudUPFGzhs4q9UTVrq2lS9Xp1MxyQa54ClrmBjpsGdLRNcdjcHVQPKwJGxmuMIYuPvBzU9njlug7Lz-iR_2jxQZoPZPDgT0tIyJ3BwLraiTXigSumH1bc9Wbxv2sOSW9ZJQvDTbNfNqCsqCF3_KWTyjC9Mh24sYj7V8B08xa0Hs3AKxkX52F6xkRzvkjP6683wQabH_CmRw5VezkBeUtgassl_k7jwA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=%7B%5Cboldsymbol%20%5Ctau%7D%20%3D%20-%7B%5Cbf%20D%7D(%7B%5Cboldsymbol%20%5CLambda%7D%20%7B%5Cboldsymbol%20%5Cmu%7D)\" alt=\"{\\boldsymbol \\tau} = -{\\bf D}({\\boldsymbol \\Lambda} {\\boldsymbol \\mu})\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">where <img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/_0SseM4p9y6MYQkS3dTcrD0WZzjXV3nf_KKRi7zdaz8BsSSwunji12oNxbXU35aihuX5WolAFVXFJ2U9wxnFjytINh3-0ElX001Lubi7LV0=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=%7B%5Cbf%20D%7D\" alt=\"{\\bf D}\"> is a diagonal matrix with 1/sqrt(2) in the diagonals, based on the factor loadings matrix <img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/NYe5jREbKy8NQNwOkfywulTpRIGjAc7TpA2-s2edX-MquJ8XosqzPPn-ibUH_RvgWoxyJrc_g_Fv7VSyM7wmWzTWhsMINdluJt5W7E31xI6ra2mq3oDQzSMY=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=%5Cboldsymbol%20%5CLambda\" alt=\"\\boldsymbol \\Lambda\"> and the specified covariance of the latent variables, which is just the identity matrix. What is happening under the hood to estimate the means and how do I get from the means to the thresholds? The thresholds seem right based on some post-hoc inspection, but I haven’t figured out how to recover the original means (or at least the spacing among them). </p>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248);display:block\">mean(pairs_dat$i1i2)\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># first threshold looks good</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>- pnorm(-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0.772</span>)\r\n</span></span>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em\">Thanks!</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGVsbG8sPGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5JIGFtIHRyeWluZyB0byBmaWd1cmUgb3V0IGhvdyB0\nbyBzcGVjaWZ5IGEgc2ltcGxlIGxhdGVudCB2YXJpYWJsZSBtb2RlbCBmb3IgcmFua2luZyBkYXRh\nIGluIGBsYXZhYW5gIGJhc2VkIG9uIFtNYXlkZXUtT2xpdmFyZXMgYW5kIEJvY2tlbmhvbHQsIDIw\nMDVdKDEwLjEwMzcvMTA4Mi05ODlYLjEwLjMuMjg1KS4gSSBhbSB3b25kZXJpbmcgaWYgSSBhbSBt\naXNzaW5nIHNvbWUgY29uc3RyYWludHMgb3Igc29tZSBzY2FsaW5nIGZhY3RvcnMgYmVjYXVzZSB0\naGUgbWVhbiBzdHJ1Y3R1cmUgZG9lc24ndCBtYXRjaCB3aGF0IEkgYW0gZXhwZWN0aW5nLiBIZXJl\nIGFyZSB0aGUgZGV0YWlsczo8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiMjIFNpbXVsYXRpb25z\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5JIGZpcnN0IHNpbXVsYXRlZCBzb21lIGxhdGVudCB1\ndGlsaXRpZXMgZnJvbSBpbmRlcGVuZGVudCBub3JtYWxzIHdpdGggdW5pcXVlIG1lYW5zIGFuZCB2\nYXJpYW5jZXMgZXF1YWwgdG8gMS4gSSB0aGVuIGNvbnZlcnRlZCB0aGVzZSB0byByYW5rcyBiYXNl\nZCBvbiB0aGUgb3JkZXIgc3RhdGlzdGljcy4gRnJvbSB0aGVyZSwgSSBjcmVhdGVkIG9yZGVyZWQg\naW5kaWNhdG9ycyBiYXNlZCBvbiBwYWlycy4gVGhhdCBpcywgaWYgaXRlbSAxIGlzIHJhbmtlZCBh\naGVhZCBvZiBpdGVtIDIsIHRoZSBpbmRpY2F0b3IgaTFpMiBnZXRzIGEgMSwgYW5kIHplcm8gb3Ro\nZXJ3aXNlLjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YGBgcjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+c2V0LnNlZWQo\nNTY2Myk8YnI+bXUgJmx0Oy0gYygtNCwgLTIsIC0xLCAwKTxicj48YnI+cmFua3MgJmx0Oy0gc2Fw\ncGx5KDxicj4mbmJzcDsgMToxMDAsPGJyPiZuYnNwOyBmdW5jdGlvbih4KXs8YnI+Jm5ic3A7ICZu\nYnNwOyBzICZsdDstIHJub3JtKGxlbmd0aChtdSksIG1lYW4gPSBtdSk8YnI+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNw\nOyByZXR1cm4ob3JkZXIocykpPGJyPiZuYnNwOyB9PGJyPikgfCZndDsgdCgpPGJyPjxicj4jIGdp\ndmUgbmFtZXM8YnI+Y29sbmFtZXMocmFua3MpICZsdDstIHBhc3RlMCgiaSIsIDE6NCk8YnI+IyBj\ncmVhdGUgaW5kZXhlczxicj5pbmRleGVzICZsdDstIGxpc3QoKTxicj5mb3IoaSBpbiAxOihuY29s\nKHJhbmtzKSAtIDEpKXs8YnI+Jm5ic3A7IGZvcihqIGluIChpKzEpOm5jb2wocmFua3MpKXs8YnI+\nJm5ic3